description.narrative:
1 - 1 (one) Policy brief containing the main findings of the review of social protection programmes in Paraguay with a focus on its performance in reaching out to artisanal fishing communities;
2 - 1 (one) Policy brief containing a socioeconomic profile of artisanal fishers in Paraguay;
3 - 1 (one) Document with recommendations on how to strengthen interoperability of the fisher’s registry in Paraguay;
4 - 1 (one) Detailed Narrative progress report with preliminary results; 

5 - 1 (one) Evaluation report and Policy brief;

6 - 1 (one) Report on meetings to disseminate research findings;

7 - 1 (one) Report on the main features of financial compensation for fishers during closed fishing season, drawing from international experience;

8 - 1 (one) Report on the impacts of the new registration process for the RGP;

9 - 1 (one) Report on feasibility of alternative approaches to increase social protection coverage and adequacy for small-scale fishers in Tunisia;

10 - 1 (one) Policy brief on social protection performance for artisanal fishers in Tunisia.

comment.narrative:
1 - Need for comprehensive assessment of the Fishers Assistance Programme of the Social Development Ministry in Paraguay (Programa de Asistencia a Pescadores del Ministerio de Desarrollo Social);
2 - Need for assessment of # relevant international experiences with financial compensation for fishers during closed fishing seasons to inform potential reforms of Brazil’s fishers unemployment benefit (Seguro Defeso);
3 - Demand for # studies including a set of recommendations to support policy reforms for reducing poverty and vulnerabilities of small-scale fishers based on the assessment of the performance of social protection programmes as well as of fisheries and aquaculture policies and programmes in Tunisia.

